    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies that calling {@code remove()} on a {@link BoundedIterator} before any call to {@code next()} throws an {@link IllegalStateException} with the message \"remove() cannot be called before calling next()\". <p>This tests the precondition guard in {@code BoundedIterator.remove()}: even when an offset is supplied (which internally advances the underlying iterator during construction), the caller must still invoke {@code next()} at least once before {@code remove()} is permitted.</p>"
